# Normalize line endings to LF in the repository regardless of a developer
# machine's own core.autocrlf setting. Several generated/vendored files
# here (vendoredLibraries.generated.ts, xterm.js/css, marked.min.js, etc.)
# get rewritten by local build scripts with plain \n -- on a machine with
# core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) and no .gitattributes, that made
# every one of them show as "modified" after any build even though the
# content never actually changed (confirmed via `git diff -w` showing zero
# real diff, LF-vs-CRLF only).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Real binary assets -- never text-normalized, regardless of the blanket
# rule above.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
